{
  "requirement": "A record produced by finishing an SDK assessment context MUST include the\nidentity and fingerprint of every node successfully read through its assessment\ncontext, whether requested by\nordinary code or a model tool. The recorded fingerprint MUST describe the\ncontent supplied by that read.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.node_inputs`:**\n1. A record from finishing the context includes the node identity and fingerprint of every node successfully read through the context.\n2. This holds for reads by ordinary code and for reads by a model tool.\n3. The recorded fingerprint describes the content that read supplied.\n4. Failed reads add nothing, because only successful reads count.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Ordinary code reads.** `tests/validation.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` reads node 1 through `read` and `read_snapshot`. It asserts the fingerprint is `fp(\"before\")`. After the content changes it reads again and asserts a second, distinct `Dependency::Node(1, fp(\"after\"))`. The failed `read(&2)` adds no dependency. `finish` is called and `record.dependencies` is asserted equal to the observed dependencies. This covers obligations 1, 3 and 4 for ordinary code.\n- **Queued ordinary-code reads.** `tests/validation.rs#fn[later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace]` uses `current_node_contents`. It asserts `Dependency::Node(1, fp(\"retained\"))` is recorded. It also asserts the trace survives a later call and appears in the `finish` record.\n- **Model tool reads.** `tests/agent.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` has the model call `read_node` on an 18,000-character node, which spans several pages. It asserts the recorded `Dependency::Node(Node(2), …)` fingerprint equals the full content. This shows the fingerprint describes the supplied content, not just a page. It also asserts that the record equals the observations. Its failed-conversation cases check that a run failing before delivery records nothing. They also check that a read made through `current_node_contents` is still recorded when the ask fails.\n- **Source tool reads.** `tests/agent.rs#fn[cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input]` reads `fn[observed]` through `read_source`. It asserts exactly one `Dependency::Node(Node(7), …)`, whose value equals the selected content. A `read_source` of the missing selector `fn[missing]` adds no dependency.\n\n**Notes**\n- Implementation was read only to see how delivery is recorded. `read_snapshot` records the fingerprint of the snapshot it returns. The tool path uses `prepare_read` and then `delivered()` to call `observe_read`. This matches what the tests assert.\n- In the failed-conversation case a tool read is not recorded because the model never received it. That is a defensible reading of \"content supplied by that read\", and the test asserts it consistently.\n- `tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` also asserts node dependencies for `successors_content` reads. It has no `{test}` reference to this requirement. This is a minor marking omission, not an assertion gap. The marked tests already cover every distinct read path and failure case the text names.\n\nI found no unacknowledged adequacy gap.",
